							Board of  Canvassers						










									The Board of Canvassers certifies election results by reviewing and validating votes, resolving disputes, and ensuring the adherence to election laws. Comprising appointed or elected officials, the board plays a crucial role in upholding the integrity and transparency of the democratic process. Its primary duty is to officially declare and certify the final election results.								











